/*
 * K114s (MacBook Pro 14-inch, M5 Pro, Mac17,13) camera trial tree on the r3d includes: the configured tree
 * t6050-k114s-r3d.dts (a0897a5a), unchanged, plus one property on the camera (docs/r3-camera.md).
 *
 * The camera nodes (isp0 and its three DARTs, from t6050-isp.dtsi) stay disabled here, as in the configured
 * tree. The boot loader enables them only after it has read isp0's segments from the ADT and found this board's
 * row (apple,k114s 0xba on 27.2: patches/aura/camera/0001). Without that row the camera stays off, harmlessly.
 *
 * The K114s ADT describes no camera-light pin (eic cil without a cil-gpio-offset, as on the K114c), so the T6050
 * ISP driver refuses to probe without one. The owner chose (2026-11-24) to run the camera with the display's
 * best-effort camera indicator instead of a verified light: apple,camera-light-undescribed tells the r3e driver
 * (patches/linux/r3e/0075) to run this ISP with no light control.
 */
#include "t6050-k114s-r3d.dts"

&isp0 {
	apple,camera-light-undescribed;
};
